{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Melchizedek king of Shalem.</b> This is Shem son of Noah. And he was priest to El Elyon. By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'priest' means one who serves; and since among all the nations there are priests who minister to the angels called Elohim, as it is written (Exodus 15:11) ״מי כמוכה באלים ה׳״, therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, is called El Elyon — for He is supreme above all Elohim and exalted above all exalted ones. And according to the view of our Rabbis, blessed be their memory, he was an actual priest, and therefore Abraham gave him tithe, as it is written: ״ויתן לו מעשר מכל״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:22.428672347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}